tests/golden/check/ffi-lent-is-read-on-a-lend-and-nowhere-else.hero:37:19: error[lent_shape]: `lent` on `buf` of `fill` is a word nothing reads — `buf` is a `ptr` that declares no extent, and a `ptr` lend reaches only a parameter declared `counted_by` — nothing is ever lent here, so the word is dead text; write `counted_by <n> lent`
tests/golden/check/ffi-lent-is-read-on-a-lend-and-nowhere-else.hero:42:20: error[lent_shape]: `lent` on `out` of `grab` is a word nothing reads — `out` is an `@` out-parameter, and no lend can stand in an `@` position
tests/golden/check/ffi-lent-is-read-on-a-lend-and-nowhere-else.hero:46:19: error[lent_shape]: `lent` on `n` of `bump` is a word nothing reads — `n` is not a `cstr` or a `ptr`, and only those two are ever lent
tests/golden/check/ffi-lent-is-read-on-a-lend-and-nowhere-else.hero:51:20: error[lent_shape]: `lent` on `db` of `close` is a word nothing reads — `db` is not a `cstr` or a `ptr`, and only those two are ever lent
